I'll read the review brief first, then the full motion bundle, and answer only from a motion-design lens.{"lens":"Motion design and animation craft","verdict":"changes_requested","summary":"Kill ambient parallax and perpetual Terra orbit; keep one purposeful assembly, first-view only (~700ms), then instant settle with on-demand replay.","tension_rulings":[{"tension":1,"ruling":"change","why":"Z-as-depth only earns motion when assembly uses it as a climb; static Z plus ambient drift teaches nothing row position and S-tokens do not."},{"tension":3,"ruling":"change","why":"Assembly teaches once as staggered build-order; replaying full fly-in on every protocol select among twelve is theatre and fatigue."},{"tension":5,"ruling":"keep","why":"Reduced-motion and non-3D users get the full product via instant dim, numbers 1..n, and static cycle diagram—no lesser content, only no continuous motion."}],"findings":[{"id":"F1","severity":"high","section":"Part 2 — Proposed motion §2 Depth parallax","problem":"Ambient camera drift with no input taxes attention and battery on a reference tool left open while reading; it sells depth without teaching anything new.","instruction":"Remove all idle/ambient parallax. Depth is shown by row, S-token, and optional one-shot assembly climb only.","basis":"principle"},{"id":"F2","severity":"high","section":"Part 2 — Proposed motion §1 Assembly","problem":"Users will select ~12 protocols in a row; a full re-assembly each time turns the only useful motion into noise after the second viewing.","instruction":"First assembly in a session: 600–800ms total, stagger 40–60ms per step in build order, ease-out, skippable (Esc/click settles instantly). Second+ selection of any protocol: 0–120ms dim+number only. Full assembly is replay-on-demand (explicit control), never auto-replay.","basis":"principle"},{"id":"F3","severity":"high","section":"Part 2 — Proposed motion §3 The reflexive loop","problem":"A smooth continuous orbit reads as stable recursion; Terra’s loop accelerated and terminated. Perpetual motion mis-teaches the hazard.","instruction":"Replace orbit with a finite death-spiral: 2–3 cycles that tighten and speed up (~1.2–1.8s total), then a hard break/freeze on the failed state. No loop. Reduced-motion: static cycle path + break mark, no animation.","basis":"principle"},{"id":"F4","severity":"medium","section":"Part 2 — Proposed motion §4 Arrangement change","problem":"3D re-form between by-depth and by-family is pure spectacle; 2D FLIP already preserves object continuity without fighting scanability.","instruction":"Cut 3D arrangement re-form. Use short 2D FLIP (≤250ms) or instant reflow; spend the motion budget only on assembly.","basis":"principle"},{"id":"F5","severity":"medium","section":"Part 2 — Proposed motion ranking (craft)","problem":"Four motions are proposed as equal; only one carries semantic load under repeated use.","instruction":"Rank and ship: (1) keep assembly with F2 rules—most earns its place; (2) ambient parallax is pure theatre—cut; (3) Terra continuous orbit—cut outright and replace per F3; (4) 3D arrangement re-form—cut.","basis":"principle"},{"id":"F6","severity":"medium","section":"Part 2 — gap vs data (asynchrony/build order)","problem":"Numbered 1..n already static; motion that only flies tiles in that order wastes the asynchrony signal in the data.","instruction":"If assembly stays: co-arrive concurrent steps (same stagger slot), sequence only true prerequisites. That is the strongest motion idea not in the brief—asynchrony as shared vs sequential arrival—not another camera trick.","basis":"principle"},{"id":"F7","severity":"low","section":"Part 2 — single-animation constraint","problem":"Without a hard cap, decorative motions will re-enter during polish.","instruction":"If only one product animation is allowed: constrained protocol assembly (F2+F6). It alone turns build order into time and uses depth as climb. Everything else stays static.","basis":"principle"}],"what_to_keep":"Protocol assembly as a short, first-view (or on-demand) staggered build-order climb through depth—not ambient 3D décor.","dissent_note":"Spatial/3D lenses will defend ambient parallax as necessary to ‘feel’ Z; a11y will push even harder for zero auto-motion."}
